        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "What the supplied evidence recommends",
            "content": "Aishwarya Naresh Reganti says that as implementation becomes very cheap, builders should focus on design, judgment, and taste. Kiriti Badam recommends starting small to stay focused on the problem rather than the complexity of the AI solution; Reganti adds that teams should build flywheels to improve over time. Separately, John Zeratsky cautions that AI-assisted products can become generic, so speed alone is not enough—distinctiveness matters. These are recommendations from the cited speakers, not an evidenced statement by Alexander Embiricos.",
            "citation_ids": [
